# Test fixture images.
#
# Screen 3 needs photographs of real faces to exercise the face detector, and a
# drawn or synthetic face does not reliably trigger a detector trained on
# photographs. Real photographs of real people carry licensing and likeness
# questions that a committed fixture should not decide silently, and
# test-screens/README.md sets a synthetic-data-only rule for everything that is
# version controlled.
#
# So the images stay local. Supply your own and name them as below to run
# Screen 3; see test-screens/README.md.
test-screens/face-a.jpg
test-screens/face-b.png

# Python environment and caches for the backend.
server/.venv/
server/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
Shield_*_Idea_Presentation.pdf

# Provider credentials. The server reads these from the environment and nothing
# here ever needs a file — but a key committed once is a key leaked forever, so
# the pattern is ignored defensively rather than relying on nobody creating one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
